<p>King Charles III addressed a joint session of the U.S. Congress on Tuesday during a four-day state visit to the United States with Queen Camilla, becoming the first British sovereign to speak to Congress since Queen Elizabeth II in 1991. The visit marked the 250th anniversary of American independence from Britain and included a White House welcome by President Trump and first lady Melania Trump, an Oval Office meeting and a state banquet. Charles used the speech to describe the U.S.-U.K. relationship as &quot;truly unique&quot; and called for &quot;reconciliation and renewal,&quot; while acknowledging &quot;times of great uncertainty&quot;. Trump told Charles at the White House that Americans have had &quot;no closer friends than the British&quot; and said the two countries had a &quot;special relationship&quot; he hoped would remain. The ceremonial visit followed months of strain between Washington and London over Trump&#x27;s war with Iran, his frustrations with NATO, bilateral trade tensions and his criticism of British Prime Minister Keir Starmer. In Congress, Charles cited NATO&#x27;s invocation of Article 5 after the Sept. 11 attacks and said &quot;that same, unyielding resolve is needed for the defense of Ukraine and her most courageous people,&quot; according to Politico.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/oVOf3H0JX79q4yiEKeok7T50AwC4Y2JmUwmXwLK1npB5On8g8UVPFrKWMoLOH9uo7Lenytjfjv-ZlAATJwhrRcdsEOU1ODDVXmRrkZbLm5BQNoqkI0kP5AxlNGu4SMNoxvcCvTIMCHMArNBwL6V3C8LUhzyVS3A7LNcjQMIxJygtDTPHgJptZJbZAJC_1yz-XzqUR95jf5eQ3ShsK644lzPlR7Q37gXpX69VsqRZnLf4O07gtIQFPBiDetX0T0Pco-8dGHEemPwiuCYSBA' alt='U.S. Vice-President JD Vance and House Speaker Mike Johnson applaud King Charles during his speech to Congress.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Security backdrop: The royal itinerary proceeded after plans were reviewed following a shooting at the White House Correspondents&#x27; Association dinner days earlier.</li><li>Congress forum: The invitation added Charles to the list of foreign figures who have addressed Congress, including Pope Francis, Václav Havel and Winston Churchill.</li><li>Reign milestone: It was Charles&#x27;s first trip to the United States since becoming king in 2022 and the first visit to the country by a British monarch in two decades.</li><li>Ceremonial welcome: The White House event included a South Lawn military welcome, cannon fire and a 21-gun salute before private talks.</li></ul><blockquote>Time and again, our two countries have always found ways to come together - King Charles III</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump joked under gray, drizzly skies that it was a &quot;beautiful British day.&quot; (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/watch-trump-welcomes-king-charles-to-the-white-house-on-his-day-of-diplomacy-in-washington'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>King Charles III: Charles said the alliance could not &quot;rest on past achievements,&quot; saying inherited ties had to be applied to present challenges. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/28/trump-hails-british-friends-as-king-visits_6752942_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>House Speaker Mike Johnson: Johnson, who became the first sitting House speaker to address the U.K. Parliament earlier in 2026, said ahead of Charles&#x27;s speech that the king would be &quot;well received&quot; in Congress. (<a href='https://www.kron4.com/news/king-charles-iii-will-meet-trump-address-congress-in-a-bid-to-spotlight-uk-us-ties/'>KRON4</a>)</li><li>Politico: Politico described the 9/11 passage as coded royal diplomacy and a rebuff to Trump-aligned skepticism of NATO and Western unity. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2026/04/28/king-charles-washington-visit/charles-challenges-trump-nato-ukraine-speech-00896491'>Politico</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-28-0700/foreign-policy-us-uk-friction-forms-backdrop-kings-speech'>US-UK friction forms 